// RtOp, collections: Lists, maps, sets, bytes, `Shared`, raw memory and drops. Read by `compiler/kir/build.rs`.
ListLen,
ListIsEmpty,
ListPush,
ListGet,
ListFirst,
ListLast,
ListContains,
/// `list[i] = v`; panics when out of range.
ListSet,
/// `xs.pop()`'s second half: the list cut to its first `n` items, in
/// place when nothing else holds it (spec 14.2).
ListTruncate,
MapGet,
MapInsert,
MapRemove,
MapContains,
MapLen,
MapIsEmpty,
MapKeys,
MapValues,
/// The entries as a list of `(key, value)` tuples, for `for`.
MapEntries,
SharedNew,
SharedGet,
SharedSet,
/// `update` takes and lets go of the value's lock around its function
/// (decision 0052).
SharedLock,
SharedUnlock,
ListJoin,
ListSort,
/// Sorts the list (first operand) by the keys in the second list.
ListSortBy,
ListReverse,
ListTake,
ListSkip,
ListIndexOf,
ListMin,
ListMax,
/// `map[key] ?? fallback` for a scalar value and a fallback that is a
/// constant or a local: the value, or the fallback (nothing boxed).
MapGetOr,
/// `Bytes` (spec 2.13): from a list, from text, `b[i]` (which panics
/// out of range), its methods, `a + b`; and `std.fs` for bytes, which
/// can fail.
BytesNew,
BytesAt,
BytesLen,
BytesGet,
BytesSlice,
BytesText,
BytesToList,
BytesAsList,
BytesConcat,
BytesCrc32c,
/// Raw memory (spec 6.4, `lower_ptr.rs`): `alloc` (count, item size)
/// and `free`, C's own; a load from and a store to an address the
/// compiler worked out, which the backends inline; and a text copied
/// for C with a zero byte after it (10.7), freed after the call; and
/// C's text at an address, copied (`none` for a null pointer).
PtrAlloc,
PtrFree,
PtrRead,
PtrWrite,
PtrText,
PtrReadText,
/// A chunked loop on all cores (decision 0031): the backends call
/// `kv_par_for`, or give 1 ("run the plain loop yourself").
ParFor,
/// A chunked integer reduction (decision 0031): `kv_par_for_red`,
/// whose chunks also get a slot number for their partial sums.
ParForRed,
/// `on cores(n)` and `on threads(n)` before a loop (spec 4.9): panics
/// when the count `a` is under 1 (`b` is 1 for threads). `par.rs` passes
/// the same count to the loop's `kv_par_for`, its most cores.
ParCores,
/// `Map.capacity(n, first)` (spec 2.2): a map of at most `a` entries,
/// `b` its first ones (0: none).
MapCapacity,
/// `List.capacity(n, first)` (spec 2.2): a list of at most `a` items,
/// with room for them all, `b` its first ones (0: none).
ListCapacity,
/// `b.xxhash64()` (spec 2.13).
BytesXxhash64,
/// A hint that item `b` of list `a` will be read soon (`prefetch.rs`):
/// nothing a program sees; a backend may ignore it.
ListPrefetch,
/// A hint that integer key `b` of map `a` will be looked up soon
/// (`prefetch.rs`): its bucket is asked for.
MapPrefetch,
/// At the start of a program with `Drop` (spec 6.1): type number `a`
/// runs closure `b` (its `drop`) when its last holder ends.
DropRegister,
/// At a statement boundary: run the `drop` of the values whose last
/// holder has ended (`runtime/native/src/rt_drops.rs`).
DropRun,
/// `b.index_of(part)` on `Bytes` (spec 2.13).
BytesIndexOf,
/// `s.weak()` and `w.shared()` (spec 6.2): a `Weak` has the shape of
/// its `Shared`, around a weak cell (`runtime/native/src/send.rs`).
WeakMake,
WeakShared,
/// `Bytes` (owned) copied for C (spec 10.7), and `p.bytes(n)`: `n` bytes
/// at `p` copied out (spec 6.4).
PtrBytes,
PtrReadBytes,
/// `b.read<T>(at, big_endian)` and `Bytes.of<T>(n, big_endian)` (spec
/// 2.13): `read`'s result type names `T`; `of` gets the size of `T`.
BytesRead,
BytesOfNumber,
/// `std.matrix` (spec 2.17, `runtime/native/src/rt_matrix.rs`), on flat
/// lists of numbers, the result a list of type `code`: the product of `a`
/// and `b` with the sizes and `fast` in list `c`; `a` and `b` item by item
/// (`c`: 0 add, 1 subtract, 2 multiply); `a` scaled by `b`; `a` negated;
/// `a` transposed, and its sums (all, by row, by column), with the sizes in
/// list `b`.
MatrixProduct,
MatrixZip,
MatrixScale,
MatrixNegate,
MatrixTranspose,
MatrixSums,
/// `Set.capacity(n, first)` (spec 2.2): a set of at most `a` entries,
/// the list `b` its first ones (0: none).
SetCapacity,
/// `xs.is_full()` (spec 2.2): a list made by `List.capacity(n)` holding
/// `n` items.
ListIsFull,
/// `m.is_full()` for a map or set (spec 2.2).
MapIsFull,
/// `xs` for `xs + ys`: the list itself, or a copy without its limit
/// when it has one, since a new list has none (spec 2.2).
ListNoLimit,
/// `Ring.capacity(n, first)` (spec 2.2): a list of at most `a` items that
/// drops its oldest when full, the list `b` its first ones (0: none).
RingCapacity,
/// At the start of a program with `Display` types (spec 1.11): type
/// number `a` shows as closure `b` (its `display`) gives.
DisplayRegister,
/// `b.text(start, end)` and `b.slice(start, end).text()` on `Bytes`
/// (spec 2.13): the range `b..c`, clamped, as text, copied once.
BytesTextRange,
